BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (Play 8, deadline control, implements distinct clocks instead of one generic thirty-day task. Under the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (baseline federal process, a party generally initiates open negotiation within 30 business days after receiving) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (the initial payment or denial. The open-negotiation period then lasts 30 business days; federal IDR generally) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (must be initiated within four business days after that period ends. The four-day window is not a universal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (entity-selection or batching deadline. Record receipt evidence, negotiation delivery, calendar definitions,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (holidays, portal acknowledgments, and any authorized extension. Implement the clock in a versioned state) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (machine with a second-person check rather than trusting a spreadsheet formula copied between) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (jurisdictions. The 90-calendar-day cooling-off restriction concerns the initiating party bringing subsequent) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (disputes involving the same other party and same or similar items or services after a determination; it is not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (a blanket ninety-day suspension of all payer work. The statute also provides a subsequent initiation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (opportunity for affected claims. Maintain a linked cooling-off register and calculate the applicable post-period) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (window. Check current regulations, controlling court orders, and CMS implementation instructions before) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (relying on operational batching criteria or portal procedures. Store the version used, because a historically) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (correct workflow can become wrong after an implementation change.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (Play 9, evidence construction, distinguishes permissible claim-specific support from prohibited arbitration) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (inputs. The statute directs consideration of the QPA and specified additional information, while excluding) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (usual and customary charges, billed charges, and public-program reimbursement rates as payment) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm (determinants. Do not instruct a brief builder to multiply a FAIR Health charge percentile and present the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm (result as a permissible federal IDR valuation. Identify the licensed dataset, its actual measure, the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.72 Tm (evidentiary proposition, and whether that use is permissible before including any benchmark. Clinical acuity,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 411.50 Tm (patient complexity, training, facility characteristics, and documented contracting efforts need claim-specific) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 396.27 Tm (support and careful treatment of information already reflected in the QPA. CARC and RARC values help) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 381.05 Tm (classify remittances but cannot prove jurisdiction, clinical complexity, or an incorrect QPA independently.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.82 Tm (Use templates to assemble exhibits, then require a qualified reviewer to verify every assertion and source.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 350.60 Tm (For batching, evaluate the operative statutory and regulatory conditions, including relevant party, service,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 335.37 Tm (coding, and service-period requirements, rather than assuming one payer name makes all claims) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 320.15 Tm (compatible. When compatibility is uncertain, split supported cases or obtain clarification before filing. A) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 304.92 Tm (cheaper aggregate submission is expensive if dismissal destroys its expected recovery and consumes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 289.70 Tm (unrecoverable fees.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 274.47 Tm (Play 10, cash reconciliation, tracks submitted offer, determination, payment due date, actual receipt, fee) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 259.25 Tm (refund, and recoupment as different ledger events. The federal statute generally requires payment within 30) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 244.02 Tm (calendar days after the determination; an overdue award belongs in a documented collection escalation, not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 228.80 Tm (in cash revenue. The administrative fee is nonrefundable. In an ordinary completed determination, the) Tj ET
